    </seriesStmt><sourceDesc><p>Born digital.</p></sourceDesc></fileDesc><revisionDesc><change who="http://syriaca.org/documentation/editors.xml#autogenerated" when="2026-07-28-05:00">CREATED: This bibl record was autogenerated from a Zotero record.</change><change who="https://www.zotero.org/cbss_admin" when="2022-11-18T14:31:51Z">Record created in Zotero.</change></revisionDesc></teiHeader><text><body><biblStruct type="journalArticle"><analytic><author><forename>Héctor Ricardo</forename><surname>Francisco</surname></author><title level="a">The Old Testament in the First Discourse on Martyrs</title><idno type="URI">http://syriaca.org/cbss/X6B6KXNC</idno><idno type="URI">https://www.zotero.org/groups/a_comprehensive_bibliography_on_syriac_studies/items/X6B6KXNC</idno><idno type="URI">https://www.zotero.org/groups/4861694/items/X6B6KXNC</idno></analytic><monogr><title level="j">Scrinium</title><imprint><date>2021</date></imprint><biblScope unit="vol">17</biblScope><biblScope unit="pp">110-133</biblScope></monogr><note type="abstract">The aim of this paper is to analyze the use of Biblical Testimonia in the &lt;i&gt;First Discourse of the Holy Martyrs of the Land of Orient&lt;/i&gt; (BHO 706). It will be argued that the main purpose of the author was not only to promote the cult of their relics but also to demonstrate that the persecution was part of God’s plan for the Church. As long as Christ, the Apostles and the Prophets were Models for those suffering persecution, the Biblical text was the testimony of the truth of Christian Martyrdom. Moreover, by stressing the continuity between the Heroes of both Testaments and the Martyrs, the author was engaged in a controversy against Marcionism.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
  Francisco, Héctor Ricardo. “The Old Testament in the First Discourse on Martyrs.” <title level="m">Scrinium</title> 17 (2021): 110–33.
